se safety of anesthetics by advancements in anesthesia monitoring: scientometric analysis. Drug Des Devel Ther 2015;9:2599–608. 10.2147/DDDT.S81013 [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 30. Clancy CM. TeamSTEPPS: optimizing teamwork in the perioperative setting. AORN J 2007;86:20–2. 10.1016/j.aorn.2007.06.008 [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 31. Weld LR, Stringer MT, Ebertowski JS, et al. TeamSTEPPS improves operating room efficiency and patient safety. Am J Med Qual 2016;31:408–14. 10.1177/1062860615583671 [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 32. Lingard L. Communication failures in the operating room: an observational classification of recurrent types and effects. Qual Saf Heal Care 2004;13:330–4. 10.1136/qshc.2003.008425 [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 33. Hu YY, Arriaga AF, Roth EM, et al. Protecting patients from an unsafe system. Ann Surg 2012;256:203–10. 10.1097/SLA.0b013e3182602564 [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 34. Davies JM, Posner KL, Lee LA, et al. Liability associated with obstetric anesthesia: a closed claims analysis. Anesthesiology 2009;110:131–9. 10.1097/ALN.0b013e318190e16a [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 35. Lisbon D, Allin D, Cleek C, et al. Improved knowledge, attitudes, and behaviors after implementation of TeamSTEPPS training in an academic emergency department: a pilot report. Am J Med Qual 2016;31:86–90. 10.1177/1062860614545123 [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 36. Heideveld-Chevalking AJ, Calsbeek H, Damen J, et al. The impact of a standardized incident reporting system in the perioperative setting: a single center experience on 2,563 “near-misses” and adverse events. Patient Saf Surg 2014;8:46. 10.1186/s13037-014-0046-1 [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 37. Pearsall M. Makeshift jet ventilator setup. J Clin Anesth 2012;24:168–9. 10.1016/j.jclinane.2010.11.005 [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 38. Platts-Mills TF, Lewin 