1. Thibault S., Barbarat P., Leroy F., Bernard B.A. Human hair keratin network and curvature. Int J Dermatol. 2007;46:7S–10S. doi: 10.1111/j.1365-4632.2007.03454.x. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 52. Tucker J.A. The continuing value of electron microscopy in surgical pathology. Ultrastruct Pathol. 2000;24:383–389. doi: 10.1080/019131200750060041. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 53. Lloreta-Trull J., Ferrer L., Ribalta T., Pavesi M., Serrano S. Electron microscopy in pathology articles: a retrospective appraisal. Ultrastruct Pathol. 2000;24:105–108. doi: 10.1080/01913120050118585. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 54. Brest P, Corcelle E, Cesaro A, Chargui A, Belaid A, Klionsky DJ et al. Autophagy and inflammatory bowel diseases: at the crossroads of infection, inflammation, immunity and cancer. Curr Mol Med [sous presse]. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] 55. Tasdemir E., Galluzzi L., Maiuri M.C., Criollo A., Vitale I., Hangen E. Methods for assessing autophagy and autophagice cell death. Methods Mol Biol. 2008;445:29–76. doi: 10.1007/978-1-59745-157-4_3. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 56. Curry A. Electron microscopy as a tool for identifying new pathogens. J Infect. 2000;40:107–115. doi: 10.1053/jinf.2000.0634. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 57. Curry A. Electron microscopy and the investigation of new infectious diseases. Int J Infect Dis. 2003;7:251–257. doi: 10.1016/s1201-9712(03)90103-2. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 58. Eyden B. Electron microscopy in the diagnosis of tumours. Curr Diagn Pathol. 2002;8:216–224. [ Google Scholar ] 59. Wagner B.E., Curry A. The usefulness of electron microscopy in the diagnosis of tumours. Curr Diagn Pathol. 2002;8:232–240. [ Google Scholar ] 60. Schroeder J.A., Voekl E., Hofstaeder F. Ultrastructural telepathology – remote EM-diagnostic via internet. Ultrastruct Pathol. 2001;25:301–307. doi: 10.1080/019131201753136322. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ]',6,'2025-10-15 11:35:24','