Karczewski KJ, Snyder MP. Integrative omics for health and disease. Nat Rev Genet. 2018;19:299–310. doi: 10.1038/nrg.2018.4. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 41. Lima C, Ahmed S, Xu Y, et al. Simultaneous Raman and infrared spectroscopy: a novel combination for studying bacterial infections at the single cell level. Chem Sci. 2022;13:8171–8179. doi: 10.1039/D2SC02493D. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 42. Crapnell RD, Jesadabundit W, Garcia-Miranda Ferrari A, et al. Toward the rapid diagnosis of sepsis: detecting interleukin-6 in blood plasma using functionalized screen-printed electrodes with a thermal detection methodology. Anal Chem. 2021;93:5931–5938. doi: 10.1021/acs.analchem.1c00417. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 43. Chen Q, Liang X, Wu T, et al. Integrative analysis of metabolomics and proteomics reveals amino acid metabolism disorder in sepsis. J Transl Med. 2022;20:123. doi: 10.1186/s12967-022-03320-y. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 44. Mickiewicz B, Thompson GC, Blackwood J, et al. Development of metabolic and inflammatory mediator biomarker phenotyping for early diagnosis and triage of pediatric sepsis. Crit Care. 2015;19:320. doi: 10.1186/s13054-015-1026-2. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 45. van Houten CB, de Groot JAH, Klein A, et al. A host-protein based assay to differentiate between bacterial and viral infections in preschool children (OPPORTUNITY): a double-blind, multicentre, validation study. Lancet Infect Dis. 2017;17:431–440. doi: 10.1016/S1473-3099(16)30519-9. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 46. Kauppi AM, Edin A, Ziegler I, et al. Metabolites in blood for prediction of bacteremic sepsis in the emergency room. PLoS ONE. 2016;11:e0147670. doi: 10.1371/journal.pone.0147670. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 47. Evans CR, Karnovsky A, Puskarich MA, Michailidis G, Jones AE, Stringer KA. Untargeted metabo